AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000010> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000970> "Note that whilst this is classified as an organ, it is in fact more of a unit composed of different structures: in Drosophila, it includes the interommatidial bristle as a part; we consider here the vertebrate eye to include the eyeball/eye proper as a part, with the eye having as parts (when present): eyelids, conjuctiva,")
