# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> (digestive tract)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Wikipedia:Talk:Human_gastrointestinal_tract") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://github.com/geneontology/go-ontology/issues/7549") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "A tube extending from the mouth to the anus.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "Wikipedia:Acoelomorpha") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002161> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_147099>)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "DOI:10.1371/journal.pone.0016309") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002161> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_41324>)
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002175> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_9606>)
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-08-14") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "TAO:0000112") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "TAO") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ZFIN:curator") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "The alimentary or digestive tract, and associated organs.[TAO]")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-09-17") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "VHOG:0000309") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "VHOG") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ISBN:978-0030259821 Ruppert EE, Fox RS, Barnes RD, Invertebrate zoology: a functional evolutionary approach (2003) p.203, ISBN:978-0521617147 Stevens CE and Hume ID, Comparative physiology of the vertebrate digestive system (2004) p.11") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "http://bgee.unil.ch/") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000003> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "The bilaterian gut is typically a complete tube that opens to the exterior at both ends. It consists of mouth, foregut, midgut, hindgut, and anus (reference 1); Although all vertebrates have a digestive tract and accessory glands, various parts of this system are not necessarily homologous, analogous, or even present in all species. Therefore, broad comparisons can be best made under the listings of headgut, foregut, midgut, pancreas and biliary system, hindgut (reference 2).[well established][VHOG]")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_ontology> "FMA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "FMA also has a term 'gastrointestinal tract', but this includes the liver.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_ontology> "MA") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000012> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "we place the MA and EMAPA class here, although the intent is probably a smaller region. See https://github.com/obophenotype/uberon/issues/509")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000013> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001555> "we following Kardong in naming the entire tube from mouth to anus the alimentary canal. Kardong calls the portion of this tract that excludes buccal cavity and pharynx the 'alimentary canal', consider adding an extra class for this")
