AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "ZFA:0001077") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005562> "A small outgrowth of the pharyngeal epithelium that is the site of lymphocyte cell production[ZFA]. [PMID].")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ISBN:0781714125") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000116> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005562> "we follow Kardong table 13.1 in having some developmental contribution of pouch 4 in mammals, but this isn't reflected in EHDAA2. Consider adding distinct term for mesenchyme (see EHDAA2), to indicate NC constribution.")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#date_retrieved> "2012-08-14") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#external_class> "TAO:0001077") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#ontology> "TAO") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ZFIN:curator") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000001> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005562> "A small outgrowth of the pharyngeal epithelium that is the site of lymphocyte cell production. Willett et al, 1999.[TAO]")
AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#source> "ISBN:0781714125") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBPROP_0000008> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005562> "variability of developmental origin: In fish, thymic primordia are generated by all the pouches except the first. However, in avians the thymus arises from pouches 3 and 4, whereas in humans it is only generated by the third pouch[PMID:16313389] The thymus arises from the second pouch in frogs, 2-6 in cartilaginous fish, 2-3 in reptiles, 3 or 4 in bony fish, birds and mammals. The final number is variable - 5 paired organs in sharks, 4 in caecilians, 3 in urodeles, 1 in many teleost, anurans and many mammals")
AnnotationAssertion(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0005562> "EFO:0003622")
